{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/614050-character-generation-question-relics","id":614050,"title":"Character generation question: Relics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-03T14:40:27-07:00","id":614050,"title":"Character generation question: Relics","content":"Hi everybody,<br /> <br /> this is my first time writing on the Onyx Path forum so, delighted to make your acquaintance.<br /> I picked up Scion many years ago, went through it a couple of times and gave it a try but I never really ran a chronicle.<br /> I have some questions regarding Birthrights, on the topic of the &quot;Relic&quot; merit in particular: is there a limit on how many Relics can a character have at creation? Is it a one-way/limited trait like, say, the Resources background in cWoD or can you allocate more than five points on different relics? (e.g. one 5-point and one 3-point relic or two 2-point relics)<br /> The same goes for the other Birthrights, but those are less confusing on this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7149-hateloth","name":"Hateloth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T15:32:08-07:00","id":614185,"title":"","content":"At character creation, the only limit is that you can't use your birthrights point to create one with more than 3 dots. If you want to bring it to 4 or 5, you're gonna have to use your bonus points for that. Otherwise, no, you don't have any limits. Hell, if you wanted to, you could have 20 1-dot birthrights by spending all your bonus points on it, although it would be hugely impratical.<br /> <br /> Also, welcome! Good luck on your chronicle, and not to be a downer, but if you want to run a game by using the rules as they were published, be prepared to have a hard time balancing your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T16:07:31-07:00","id":614242,"title":"","content":"I would also add that by the book, Birthrights (relics included) only go up to 5 dots. I would personally recommend increasing it to 10 or 15 dots at the demi/god boost but thats just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T16:12:40-07:00","id":614256,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer! I figured as much but wanted to be sure.<br /> May I ask you which aspects of the rules are you referring to and what do you mean by &quot;have a hard time balancing the game&quot;? Also how do you deal with the mentioned problems?<br /> <br /> I'm used to not-very-fair games like Werewolf: the apocalypse or Tribe 8 (silhouette from Dreampod-9) and I'm accustomed to their lack of balance. My group is very cohesive so I know we won't fight over rules and mechanics (not much at least). Any suggestion will be greatly appreciated though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7149-hateloth","name":"Hateloth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T19:52:49-07:00","id":614445,"title":"","content":"When the game gets to Legend 4, things start to fall apart. The Epics aren't really well-integrated into the system. So you can start getting used to no one ever, <i>ever</i> being able to fail a roll, much less botch. Guns become useless compared to archery, thrown weapons, bare hands and melee. A lot of powers based on degree of success get very, <i>very</i> strange once everyone can assume 5+ successes automatically. If you don't fix certain Knacks (like Untouchable Opponent) then combat becomes literally impossible as DVs will be so far beyond any possible attack pool that nothing will ever hit anyone again. The NPC's listed in the back as allies and antagonists will either one-shot your characters, <i>get</i> one-shot <i>by</i> your characters... or combat will be never-ending stalemates. It depends on who has which Knacks. There will be <i>numerous</i> Purviews with Knacks so useless that they're literally a waste of XP. Other Purviews will be so amazing that <i>not</i> taking them (Animal) is pretty much suicidal. <br /> <br /> As long as you stay at Hero (Legend 2, 3 and 4) things are <i>mostly</i> alright. After that... well, the game just isn't very playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T20:37:57-07:00","id":614494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/614050-character-generation-question-relics?p=614445#post614445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the game gets to Legend 4, things start to fall apart. The Epics aren't really well-integrated into the system. So you can start getting used to no one ever, <i>ever</i> being able to fail a roll, much less botch. Guns become useless compared to archery, thrown weapons, bare hands and melee. A lot of powers based on degree of success get very, <i>very</i> strange once everyone can assume 5+ successes automatically. If you don't fix certain Knacks (like Untouchable Opponent) then combat becomes literally impossible as DVs will be so far beyond any possible attack pool that nothing will ever hit anyone again. The NPC's listed in the back as allies and antagonists will either one-shot your characters, <i>get</i> one-shot <i>by</i> your characters... or combat will be never-ending stalemates. It depends on who has which Knacks. There will be <i>numerous</i> Purviews with Knacks so useless that they're literally a waste of XP. Other Purviews will be so amazing that <i>not</i> taking them (Animal) is pretty much suicidal.<br /> <br /> As long as you stay at Hero (Legend 2, 3 and 4) things are <i>mostly</i> alright. After that... well, the game just isn't very playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <b><i>really</i></b> subjective there, as you are basically saying no one every played any games that &quot;functioned&quot; above level 3. And considering I ran two games up to God with only some house rules, that's not totally true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T23:44:32-07:00","id":614644,"title":"","content":"How many House Rules is &quot;some&quot; and how extensive? The system just <i>stops working</i> by Legend 6 or 7, and that's even leaving aside the whole &quot;some Boons are game-shattering while some are worthless&quot; issue. You can get around the system fracturing by applying a few House Rules and it helps if your players know to invest mostly in Epics and avoid the terrible Boons. But that doesn't mean the game works. That doesn't mean it's well-written and fully functional out of the box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T05:43:10-07:00","id":614907,"title":"","content":"You all got me a little worried here!<br /> No, not much really. This is getting interesting, thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/614050-character-generation-question-relics?p=614445#post614445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the game gets to Legend 4, things start to fall apart. The Epics aren't really well-integrated into the system. So you can start getting used to no one ever, <i>ever</i> being able to fail a roll, much less botch. Guns become useless compared to archery, thrown weapons, bare hands and melee. A lot of powers based on degree of success get very, <i>very</i> strange once everyone can assume 5+ successes automatically. If you don't fix certain Knacks (like Untouchable Opponent) then combat becomes literally impossible as DVs will be so far beyond any possible attack pool that nothing will ever hit anyone again. The NPC's listed in the back as allies and antagonists will either one-shot your characters, <i>get</i> one-shot <i>by</i> your characters... or combat will be never-ending stalemates. It depends on who has which Knacks. There will be <i>numerous</i> Purviews with Knacks so useless that they're literally a waste of XP. Other Purviews will be so amazing that <i>not</i> taking them (Animal) is pretty much suicidal.<br /> <br /> As long as you stay at Hero (Legend 2, 3 and 4) things are <i>mostly</i> alright. After that... well, the game just isn't very playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically you're saying that we shouldn't get to the demigod/god tiers and if we do we should be paying a lot of attention to how the characters' features and knacks click together and expect to have problems; maybe we will be forced to change some of the rules (or a lot of them?). The main problem, if I got this right, are some game-breaking powers whose magnitude uncontrollably escalate when characters start piling up huge dice pools. And this is a flaw in the game design.<br /> <br /> How do I make it work the &quot;right&quot; way? Are there guidelines you can point me to or community-made material I should be looking at ? How do YOU make it functional?<br /> I'm open to any suggestion and if I have to work on it on my own I'm totally up to the task!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7149-hateloth","name":"Hateloth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T06:43:14-07:00","id":614964,"title":"","content":"I would agree with Telgar and recommend that you reduce epics to a single success per point instead of the games chart which rapidly gets out of hand. (When one 7 gives you 48 successes and 8 gives you 60, one epic makes the fight entirely unwinnable or you might as well be fighting extras.).<br /> <br /> I think it would be a feat in itself to go through all the houserules to make scion a playable and fun system that works and would recommend using scion 2.0 (Fanmade, separate from 2E). <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/\" target=\"_blank\">https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:37:09-07:00","id":615049,"title":"","content":"That seems really interesting and useful, thanks \u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar.<br /> Yeah, now that you're pointing it out I see that the Epics might turn out to be the power-creeping ultimate weapon on higher levels, scaling as they do. What about Legend? Does it pose the same threat? Should we be worried about its power getting out of hand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7149-hateloth","name":"Hateloth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T08:17:49-07:00","id":615122,"title":"","content":"Legend isn't really a concern except that it limits everything else.<br /> <br /> The big problem with Scion isn't that it can't be fixed... it's that all the fixes are essentially re-writes of the game. There are several out there. I've re-written Scion up to Demigod and slightly beyond. Twice. There's the GothamByNight rules, which are now kind of a friends-only PDF circulating online, and the Scion2 project. There's others. But each one is <i>re-writing the game</i>. <br /> <br /> Honestly, my advice is to try starting out simple and fix the problems as you run into them. Just encourage your players to stick to Epics rather than Purviews, ban or house rule Untouchable Opponent (Dex Knack) and give out Legend increases by ST fiat instead of charging XP for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:58:33-07:00","id":615520,"title":"","content":"There are a host of other little niggling problems nesting in there like baby crabs inside their mother. Such as:<br /> <br /> The game is 100% focused on grand epic combats and caters to the physical stats. The social stats get a mushy treatment where they are either outright game breakers from the get go or they are effectively useless. Mental stats are not tremendously useful. It is VERY easy to play a physical character who dabbles in social stats and be just as good in any situation as a character who devotes everything to that area. Mental characters have essentially nothing to do. The game caters to Heracles or Ares. It's not as good if you want to play Helen or Aphrodite. It's fuck all if you want to play Daedalus or Hephaestus. It works pretty good if you want to be a battler and look good doing it (Paris or Apollo) or if you want to be scrapper with a hefty dose of smarts (Odysseus or Athena). Just keep it on the fighting. Never use a gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}